WEBVTT

00:10.130 --> 00:13.200
What is it, Yukichi?

00:13.200 --> 00:16.240
I had to work on my day off yesterday.

00:16.240 --> 00:18.450
Lemme sleep today...

00:24.680 --> 00:29.800
That idol event is on 
the last Sunday of the month...

00:32.840 --> 00:34.430
Sunday...

00:39.300 --> 00:41.320
Oh, that's right. This month...

00:42.030 --> 00:43.930
Then, can I ask for a favor?

00:44.710 --> 00:47.440
O-Of course! What can I do?

00:47.440 --> 00:51.220
I want you to go to the aquarium with me 
on the last Sunday of the month.

00:53.840 --> 00:54.770
It's today!

00:56.810 --> 00:58.230
Ouch!

00:59.160 --> 01:00.850
What time is it now?!

01:17.800 --> 01:24.930
<b>The Masterful Cat
Is Depressed Again Today</b>

02:32.000 --> 02:35.670
Can

02:32.000 --> 02:35.670
<b>A Masterful Cat Goes to the Aquarium</b>

02:35.800 --> 02:37.010
<b>A Masterful Cat Goes to the Aquarium</b>

02:35.880 --> 02:37.010
Can

02:39.700 --> 02:40.840
Ten!

02:40.840 --> 02:42.340
It's still ten in the morning!

02:42.730 --> 02:46.060
Thank goodness. I can still make it.

02:46.060 --> 02:47.640
Thanks!

02:48.390 --> 02:51.650
Uh, we're meeting up at 14:00.

02:52.300 --> 02:54.940
So, I'll head out a little after 13:00.

02:56.160 --> 02:59.700
What's this smell? How nostalgic.

03:01.100 --> 03:02.480
<i>Celebratory sekihan.</i>

03:03.300 --> 03:04.620
You're wrong!

03:04.620 --> 03:07.370
This really isn't a date or anything!

03:09.610 --> 03:10.870
I'll still eat it, though.

03:11.660 --> 03:15.610
I'm just accompanying him to 
this event because he asked!

03:17.580 --> 03:18.420
Another serving!

03:19.300 --> 03:21.930
This is like an extension of work.

03:21.930 --> 03:23.500
Are you listening?

03:25.350 --> 03:28.990
But would it be weird if 
I wore a suit to the aquarium?

03:31.260 --> 03:33.230
It's my day off...

03:33.720 --> 03:35.590
It's fine to dress casually, right?

03:42.070 --> 03:46.080
<b>Worn</b>

03:43.610 --> 03:46.080
<b>Shabby</b>

03:44.370 --> 03:46.080
<b>Ratty old
loungewear</b>

03:46.670 --> 03:51.330
H-How many years has it been 
since I last bought casual clothes?

03:51.930 --> 03:55.250
I definitely can't wear my loungewear out.

03:56.530 --> 04:00.140
If only I didn't have to work yesterday!

04:00.140 --> 04:02.510
No, I would have slept. I'm sure of it.

04:02.510 --> 04:04.390
Oh! This!

04:04.390 --> 04:08.510
It's a dress I wore years ago to 
a coworker's wedding reception!

04:08.510 --> 04:09.800
Won't this work?

04:09.800 --> 04:13.020
It's not a formal dress. Luck is on my side!

04:15.830 --> 04:18.020
Meat is also on my side...

04:19.150 --> 04:21.660
Yukichi!

04:27.160 --> 04:30.480
Looks like I'll have to go in my suit today.

04:30.480 --> 04:33.160
I'll just say I had work earlier in the day.

04:35.890 --> 04:36.670
Huh?

04:38.130 --> 04:38.670
Hey!

04:40.310 --> 04:41.220
Yuki...

04:45.120 --> 04:46.390
It fits!

04:46.920 --> 04:48.600
How'd you do it?!

04:49.140 --> 04:52.680
Can you turn a pumpkin into a carriage, too?

04:53.970 --> 04:56.400
Oh, it's nothing. Nothing at all.

05:00.330 --> 05:02.370
Thank you so much, Yukichi!

05:02.370 --> 05:04.640
I'll buy you some Churu on the way home!

05:06.080 --> 05:07.160
What's that?

05:08.020 --> 05:09.160
No, thank you!

05:09.160 --> 05:14.500
Goodness! Stop acting like a mom who's 
excited about her daughter's first date!

05:14.500 --> 05:15.730
I'm off!

05:20.950 --> 05:22.760
I'll eat those when I get home.

05:22.760 --> 05:25.130
Please wrap them up and 
put them in the fridge.

05:25.610 --> 05:26.680
<i>Got it.</i>

05:28.970 --> 05:30.300
Pumpkin Carriage

05:28.970 --> 05:30.300
Pumpkin Carriage

05:32.100 --> 05:35.310
Glitter Glitter

05:33.160 --> 05:34.820
<i>Bippidi-boppidi-boo!</i>

05:36.350 --> 05:40.230
<b>Final Journey</b>

05:36.850 --> 05:38.560
<b>Ching...</b>

05:37.850 --> 05:39.810
<b>Ching...</b>

05:39.100 --> 05:40.230
<b>Ching...</b>

05:44.400 --> 05:47.240
Enoshima Station

05:56.640 --> 05:58.670
You're right on time, Fukuzawa.

05:59.450 --> 06:01.040
I'm impressed.

06:01.750 --> 06:02.960
Well, let's go.

06:05.390 --> 06:07.760
<i>Wh-Who is that?</i>

06:11.400 --> 06:12.700
I'm just messing with you.

06:13.990 --> 06:16.290
This child is my niece, Mei.

06:16.290 --> 06:20.280
My parents usually take care of her, 
but they aren't available today.

06:21.020 --> 06:23.240
So it's my turn to take her.

06:23.240 --> 06:26.250
So that's why we're at the aquarium.

06:26.250 --> 06:28.620
UMYU-Sea is coming!

06:29.070 --> 06:31.320
Yume is a huge fan of UMYU-Sea.

06:34.540 --> 06:38.410
I was pretty much forced to bring her here...

06:39.720 --> 06:42.670
But to be honest, I'm not good with children.

06:43.630 --> 06:46.670
Your offer came at the perfect time.

06:47.220 --> 06:50.810
Yume, this nice lady 
will play with you today.

06:51.270 --> 06:52.260
Yay!

06:53.050 --> 06:58.360
<i>I-I feel like he covered her ears 
just now so she wouldn't hear...</i>

06:59.640 --> 07:02.940
<i>I see. So, I'm a babysitter today.</i>

07:02.940 --> 07:06.110
<i>But I don't know how to deal 
with little kids, either.</i>

07:06.110 --> 07:07.440
<i>What should I do?</i>

07:07.440 --> 07:08.720
Big Sis!

07:10.860 --> 07:13.450
Your ribbon is so cute!

07:14.400 --> 07:15.950
<i>The sound of her heart being stolen.</i>

07:16.330 --> 07:18.880
L-Let's have fun today, Yume-chan!

07:18.880 --> 07:20.970
Come on! Let's go, Chief!

07:20.970 --> 07:22.210
Chief!

07:23.000 --> 07:25.100
Fukuzawa, you fell so easily...

07:27.010 --> 07:29.490
Yume-chan, your bag is so cute!

07:29.490 --> 07:30.970
It's a kitty purse!

07:31.290 --> 07:34.310
Yeah! I love kitties!

07:34.310 --> 07:36.100
What about you, Big Sis?

07:36.100 --> 07:37.510
Don't you have one?

07:37.510 --> 07:38.720
<i>I dug my own grave!</i>

07:38.720 --> 07:40.570
How nice!

07:41.190 --> 07:44.060
What kinda kitty is it? Is it fluffy?

07:44.500 --> 07:49.000
U-Um, he's big and black...

07:49.000 --> 07:50.500
Like that one?

07:50.500 --> 07:52.500
Eh?

07:53.020 --> 07:53.770
Hm?

07:55.530 --> 07:56.780
Huh?!

07:59.420 --> 08:01.780
Sorry, I have a call.

08:01.780 --> 08:04.730
<i>W-Wasn't that Yukichi just now?</i>

08:04.730 --> 08:05.790
<i>Why's he here?!</i>

08:05.790 --> 08:08.130
<i>And how'd he get in, anyway?!</i>

08:08.840 --> 08:11.760
<i>I need to make sure it's him 
while the chief is on the phone,</i>

08:11.760 --> 08:14.680
<i>but I can't leave Yume-chan alone!</i>

08:14.680 --> 08:16.680
Wait, what?! Yume-chan?!

08:16.680 --> 08:19.010
Such a fluffy kitty!

08:19.800 --> 08:21.180
Yume-chan!

08:21.790 --> 08:22.790
No, Yume-chan!

08:22.790 --> 08:24.490
You can't follow people you don't know!

08:24.850 --> 08:26.550
It's not a person!

08:26.550 --> 08:28.670
You can't follow kitties you don't know!

08:28.670 --> 08:32.040
Yukichi! Why're you here?!

08:33.710 --> 08:35.410
Don't click your tongue at me!

08:35.410 --> 08:37.360
How'd you get here, anyways?!

08:37.360 --> 08:38.530
Did you take the train?!

08:44.540 --> 08:47.540
Is this kitty's name Yuki-chan?

08:49.390 --> 08:51.340
I remember his name now!

08:51.340 --> 08:53.550
Now I know this kitty!

08:53.550 --> 08:55.630
Look at that!

08:55.630 --> 08:57.420
Whoa! It's way too big!

08:57.420 --> 08:58.640
Let's take a picture!

08:58.640 --> 09:01.220
Shoot! Yukichi! Run!

09:01.220 --> 09:02.470
Sorry, mister!

09:06.060 --> 09:09.020
Lemme see!

09:06.060 --> 09:09.020
Whoa! So cool!

09:10.570 --> 09:12.630
<i>Things are surprisingly okay?</i>

09:15.090 --> 09:16.570
Fishies!

09:17.220 --> 09:18.900
<i>Hey, Yukichi!</i>

09:18.900 --> 09:21.140
<i>Should you really be loitering 
around looking at fish?!</i>

09:21.140 --> 09:23.500
<i>Hurry up and leave before 
you really cause a scene!</i>

09:23.950 --> 09:25.910
Sorry, Fukuzawa.

09:25.910 --> 09:26.760
Y-Yes!

09:26.760 --> 09:27.530
<i>Crap!</i>

09:27.530 --> 09:29.790
We should head to the stage soon.

09:30.120 --> 09:31.470
Oh, yes!

09:31.470 --> 09:33.170
Welcome back!

09:35.310 --> 09:36.760
<i>H-Huh? Yukichi?!</i>

09:37.150 --> 09:39.050
<i>He's gone! Yukichi?!</i>

09:41.100 --> 09:45.060
<b>Underwater Experience Zone
</b>Feel like you're in the sea!

09:42.880 --> 09:45.910
<i>Wh-Where'd you go, Yukichi?!</i>

09:50.820 --> 09:54.900
Please line up here by twos 
for the UMYU-Sea event!

09:54.900 --> 09:57.490
The UMYU-Sea event will begin soon.

10:00.230 --> 10:02.200
Big Sis, where's the kitty?

10:03.390 --> 10:06.860
I-I wonder! Who knows?

10:07.970 --> 10:10.580
I wanna watch the show with the kitty!

10:12.090 --> 10:15.010
We can't bring a cat into the aquarium.

10:16.470 --> 10:17.420
<i>I'm so sorry!</i>

10:18.280 --> 10:22.100
Come to think of it, do you know 
anything about this group, Fukuzawa?

10:22.650 --> 10:26.520
Oh, well! I looked up 
a lot of things on Youtubo!

10:26.520 --> 10:28.810
<i>The idols of the sea!</i>

10:28.810 --> 10:32.450
Now I can sing some of the songs 
without looking at the lyrics.

10:33.400 --> 10:34.610
<i>I can do the dances, too.</i>

10:34.610 --> 10:35.990
You're so serious about everything.

10:35.990 --> 10:36.740
So mean!

10:38.110 --> 10:41.410
What do you like best about UMYU-Sea?

10:42.130 --> 10:44.370
The food, I guess?

10:45.150 --> 10:49.020
They started as characters 
from an educational show.

10:49.870 --> 10:51.580
Really?

10:52.170 --> 10:55.880
They power up by eating 
the food from the sea

10:56.230 --> 11:00.510
and fight against alien monsters called Gairai 
Beasts that want to take over the earth.

11:00.510 --> 11:05.600
There's a popular children's show 
called <i>Go! Sea Slug Rangers UMYU-Sea!!</i>

11:00.510 --> 11:05.600
<b>Sea Slug Rangers</b>

11:00.510 --> 11:05.600
<b>Sea Slug Rangers</b>

11:08.000 --> 11:10.230
<i>You recorded this show again?</i>

11:09.390 --> 11:13.110
Loves learning channels

11:10.230 --> 11:12.440
<i>That's how Yukichi knows about them!</i>

11:14.690 --> 11:18.270
<i>Yukichi suddenly disappeared. Is he okay?</i>

11:17.590 --> 11:19.830
Not yet? Not yet?

11:18.450 --> 11:21.740
<i>But really. Why did he come?</i>

11:21.740 --> 11:24.730
<i>He seemed to have thought 
I was going on a date today.</i>

11:26.420 --> 11:30.760
<i>Maybe he was worried about me and wanted 
to see what kind of man the chief is?</i>

11:30.760 --> 11:32.610
Whoa! What's that?! A cat?!

11:32.610 --> 11:35.350
Crazy! I should snap a photo!

11:35.350 --> 11:36.520
So big!

11:37.320 --> 11:41.070
Please refrain from taking any 
photographs during the show.

11:41.070 --> 11:43.550
Oh, I'm very sorry!

11:44.180 --> 11:47.850
Maybe it's a Gairai Beast 
that'll appear in the event!

11:47.850 --> 11:49.930
Oh, you're probably right!

11:52.730 --> 11:55.070
<i>What are you doing here?!</i>

11:55.070 --> 11:57.490
<i>Go home while the lights are dim!</i>

11:57.490 --> 12:00.890
<i>Don't worry about me! I'm fine!</i>

12:05.410 --> 12:07.030
<b>Sea Bunny</b>

12:07.030 --> 12:08.850
<i>So that's what he's here for!</i>

12:09.180 --> 12:11.780
Hello, Enoshima!

12:11.780 --> 12:13.330
Hello!

12:11.780 --> 12:13.330
Hello!

12:17.340 --> 12:21.510
<i>We're different from clione s!</i>

12:21.510 --> 12:22.840
<i>We're...</i>

12:22.840 --> 12:24.090
<i>We're...</i>

12:24.090 --> 12:26.600
<i>Idols of the sea!</i>

12:28.170 --> 12:31.020
<i>I can't enjoy the show 
because I'm so worried...</i>

12:31.920 --> 12:35.120
Next is our customary UMYU-Sea quiz time!

12:36.020 --> 12:39.380
If you get all the questions right, 
you can win limited edition merch!

12:39.380 --> 12:41.230
Try your best!

12:41.230 --> 12:42.960
Here we go!

12:43.490 --> 12:46.410
Raise your hands if you wanna play!

12:46.410 --> 12:48.250
Me!

12:49.410 --> 12:51.910
Me! Me!

12:50.480 --> 12:52.340
<i>Hey, now! Don't raise your hand!</i>

12:52.340 --> 12:53.020
There!

12:53.620 --> 12:57.580
Our first contestant is 
the handsome papa in a suit!

12:54.170 --> 12:57.580
Yay! It's Strawberry Milk-chan!

12:58.000 --> 12:58.900
Huh?!

13:01.440 --> 13:02.760
Here's your question!

13:02.760 --> 13:05.510
What are the names 
of the sea slugs shown here?

13:05.510 --> 13:10.410
One, Coleman's Chromodoris. Two, Tyrannodoris 
luteolineata. Three, Halgerda diaphana.

13:10.410 --> 13:11.540
<i>Chief?!</i>

13:11.850 --> 13:13.780
<i>He doesn't seem like the type 
who'd be good at this stuff,</i>

13:13.780 --> 13:16.020
<i>but he was able to answer 
without any hesitation.</i>

13:16.020 --> 13:17.490
<i>He really knows his stuff.</i>

13:18.020 --> 13:22.240
You got them all right! Congratulations!

13:22.240 --> 13:24.330
Please choose an item!

13:24.990 --> 13:25.860
I'll take this, then.

13:27.250 --> 13:29.160
Here you go, Yume.

13:30.470 --> 13:33.660
It's the live concert limited edition 
Strawberry Milk sea slug!

13:34.620 --> 13:37.000
Thank you so much, Uncle Kaoru!

13:38.280 --> 13:39.920
Is something funny, Fukuzawa-kun?

13:42.480 --> 13:45.050
Not at all, Uncle Kaoru.

13:45.050 --> 13:45.920
Shut your mouth.

13:46.690 --> 13:50.070
Thank you for today! See you again soon!

13:50.050 --> 13:52.600
Bye-bye!

13:50.070 --> 13:52.600
Bye-bye!

13:54.130 --> 13:55.640
It was so much fun!

13:55.640 --> 13:56.820
You're right.

13:57.240 --> 14:00.600
You're actually not bad 
with kids at all, are you?

14:01.020 --> 14:02.620
What are you saying?

14:02.620 --> 14:07.780
She invaded my day off. 
To me, she's a Gairai Beast.

14:08.080 --> 14:13.270
But, look, you even remember 
the things she likes!

14:14.990 --> 14:17.920
I think that's more than enough!

14:17.920 --> 14:19.670
Are you sure that's enough?

14:21.190 --> 14:24.670
Just look at how happy Yume-chan is!

14:26.820 --> 14:28.240
Lost again, Yume-chan?!

14:28.240 --> 14:29.430
Yume!

14:30.060 --> 14:31.660
Yume-chan!

14:32.460 --> 14:33.620
Yume!

14:33.620 --> 14:35.290
Where are you, Yume-chan?!

14:35.290 --> 14:36.890
I'm right here!

14:38.040 --> 14:38.860
Yume!

14:38.860 --> 14:40.900
There you are! Thank goodness!

14:41.310 --> 14:45.070
Sorry, Fukuzawa. I didn't 
realize I let go of her hand.

14:45.070 --> 14:48.320
No, I'm just glad she didn't get lost.

14:48.660 --> 14:51.240
Yume-chan, let's hold hands now.

14:52.420 --> 14:54.420
Why do you have that basket with you?

14:54.420 --> 14:56.450
I've seen that basket before...

14:56.780 --> 14:58.960
Yuki-chan gave it to me!

14:58.960 --> 15:00.410
Yuki-chan?

15:02.140 --> 15:05.460
Um, uh, a friend of mine!

15:05.460 --> 15:08.700
We happened to see him 
when you took your call.

15:09.370 --> 15:11.450
I'm so sorry!

15:11.450 --> 15:13.010
I see.

15:13.010 --> 15:14.220
Why are you apologizing?

15:14.760 --> 15:17.180
Yuki-chan said we should eat these together.

15:18.350 --> 15:22.390
Amazing. It looks just 
like the lunches you bring.

15:24.610 --> 15:26.360
Hey, Big Sis!

15:27.070 --> 15:29.220
Will you play with me again?

15:29.220 --> 15:32.450
Of course! I had a great time today!

15:33.380 --> 15:35.910
Then bring Yuki-chan with you next time!

15:35.910 --> 15:37.900
I wanna fluffy hug again!

15:37.900 --> 15:38.700
Huh?!

15:38.700 --> 15:40.330
Fluffy?

15:41.160 --> 15:43.120
I-I'll ask!

16:17.210 --> 16:18.450
Yuki-chan...

16:19.270 --> 16:22.040
Yuki-chan, are you home?

16:22.530 --> 16:24.990
The sandwiches were delicious.

16:24.990 --> 16:27.790
I can't believe you took the train 
and came all the way to the aquarium...

16:28.210 --> 16:31.760
What will you do if you make it 
on Toritter or something?

16:32.970 --> 16:34.050
What?!

16:34.050 --> 16:35.160
Yukichi!

16:35.160 --> 16:36.500
What's wrong, Yukichi?!

16:36.500 --> 16:38.640
No! Don't die!

16:52.540 --> 16:56.490
Of course you're tired. 
You overexerted yourself...

16:57.130 --> 17:00.240
Well, as long as you're safe.

17:01.710 --> 17:06.120
I haven't seen Yukichi's 
sleeping face in a while.

17:11.270 --> 17:14.170
Get some good rest tonight.

17:18.640 --> 17:22.140
The Next Morning

17:33.680 --> 17:35.840
Please forgive me!

17:37.450 --> 17:40.080
<b>She begged for her life
 using the UMYU-Sea merch
 she got for him.</b>

17:38.450 --> 17:40.080
<b>A Sea Bunny-chan
 key holder</b>

17:42.670 --> 17:46.850
<i>We're different from clione sea angels!</i>

17:46.850 --> 17:48.080
<i>We're...</i>

17:48.080 --> 17:49.460
<i>We're...</i>

17:49.460 --> 17:52.320
<i>Idols of the sea!</i>

18:02.160 --> 18:05.560
<i>All of the sea and the sky!</i>

18:06.120 --> 18:09.680
<i>UMYU-Sea is on TV again...</i>

18:06.120 --> 18:11.730
<i>We'll protect all of the earth!</i>

18:13.280 --> 18:23.060
<i>The sweets we eat after defeating all of
the Gairai Beasts are the most delicious!</i>

18:26.040 --> 18:29.800
<i>—Rangers UMYU-Sea!</i>

18:30.710 --> 18:32.630
No! No! No! No!

18:32.630 --> 18:35.560
I'm not deleting it! I'm not!

18:36.690 --> 18:38.120
<i>Lucky cat.</i>

18:41.850 --> 18:43.680
<b>Nishina</b>

18:45.400 --> 18:49.510
I wish that cat would 
really come and work here.

18:45.980 --> 18:47.400
<i>Manager's vision.</i>

18:51.150 --> 18:55.360
<i>How the heck can you say that if you're 
managing a store that sells food?</i>

18:55.670 --> 18:59.690
Our sales always go up when 
that cat visits the store.

18:59.240 --> 19:05.580
<b>Manager</b>

18:59.690 --> 19:02.860
I feel like he's a real life lucky cat.

19:02.860 --> 19:05.580
I wish he'd come every day! Seriously!

19:05.580 --> 19:09.870
Why don't you post a "hiring cats" 
flyer outside the store?

19:10.540 --> 19:11.770
That's a great idea!

19:11.770 --> 19:13.130
I was kidding.

19:13.130 --> 19:16.460
<b>Hiring Full
 and Part-Time!!</b>

19:13.130 --> 19:16.460
<b></b>Want to have a great time
 working with us?

19:13.130 --> 19:16.460
<b>No experience needed!! Cats OK!!!</b>

19:13.130 --> 19:16.460
C-Cats? What in the world...

19:14.640 --> 19:17.120
Why does it say "cats OK"?!

19:17.120 --> 19:18.760
That's so funny!

19:17.120 --> 19:20.720
<i>It trended on Toritter 
for being such a strange flyer.</i>

19:21.770 --> 19:23.060
<i>It's fine.</i>

19:24.190 --> 19:26.720
Fukuzawa, don't you have a cat?

19:26.720 --> 19:28.370
Y-Yeah...

19:28.370 --> 19:34.070
My friend's cat got fat from a lack 
of exercise. Is your cat okay?

19:34.660 --> 19:36.350
Do you have a plan for getting it exercise?

19:36.740 --> 19:38.360
Huh? Plans?

19:38.360 --> 19:41.660
Like giving it lots of toys to play with.

19:41.660 --> 19:42.860
Oh...

19:50.230 --> 19:53.220
Or maybe getting a cat tower?

19:53.220 --> 19:54.290
Uh...

20:03.300 --> 20:06.310
I don't do anything like that for my cat,

20:06.310 --> 20:09.020
but it's fine since he's free 
to go in and out as he pleases.

20:09.020 --> 20:11.080
That's not fine at all!

20:11.080 --> 20:13.020
You don't lock your doors?!

20:13.660 --> 20:15.260
<i>Can't resist.</i>

20:22.150 --> 20:24.830
My shoulders have been killing me lately...

20:24.830 --> 20:27.330
Yukichi, do we have any pain relief patches?

20:30.650 --> 20:31.930
That feels so good!

20:31.930 --> 20:35.330
I can feel it stretching out 
and your toe beans are so warm!

20:38.760 --> 20:41.070
Yeah! Put more of your weight on me!

20:41.070 --> 20:42.440
There! There! There! There!

20:42.440 --> 20:44.840
Yukichi, you could become 
a professional masseuse!

20:46.430 --> 20:47.990
Your claws! Put your claws away!

20:47.990 --> 20:49.180
I'm being stabbed!

20:49.180 --> 20:51.980
Resist that instinct!

20:52.650 --> 20:54.140
<i>Those gloves.</i>

20:56.080 --> 20:57.530
Hey, Yukichi...

20:58.160 --> 21:00.090
It's been bothering me a bit.

21:00.090 --> 21:04.320
The gloves you use when dealing with 
water aren't made for humans, right?

21:06.050 --> 21:07.810
No one sells anything like them, right?

21:09.560 --> 21:11.080
Wait, does that mean...

21:11.160 --> 21:18.080
<b>Super Water Repellent</b>

21:11.330 --> 21:12.790
Spread...

21:11.880 --> 21:13.890
Whoa! You have materials to make them!

21:13.120 --> 21:18.080
Stretchy Water Repellent Base

21:13.890 --> 21:18.080
I've heard of foxes buying mittens, 
but never a cat making gloves!

21:18.080 --> 21:19.910
Huh?! Is this a pattern?!

21:19.910 --> 21:21.680
You even made a pattern for it?!

21:23.580 --> 21:25.360
You should open up a store!

21:25.360 --> 21:28.010
A specialty shop for large cats!

21:28.220 --> 21:31.890
A job Yukichi ought to do

21:31.890 --> 21:35.380
Okay, everyone. Let's go!

21:33.060 --> 21:36.020
Childcare Worker

23:06.980 --> 23:32.680
<b>Next Episode</b>

23:07.470 --> 23:10.150
<i>I am a masterful cat.</i>

23:10.570 --> 23:12.640
<i>A masterful cat knows.</i>

23:13.170 --> 23:17.640
<i>There are tricks to make food 
taste delicious even when it's cold.</i>

23:18.130 --> 23:21.870
<i>Pick lean meats, so the fat doesn't harden.</i>

23:22.400 --> 23:27.090
<i>Food tastes blander when it's cold,
so add more seasoning than you typically would.</i>

23:27.090 --> 23:29.340
<i>These are a few ways to 
make cold food more delicious.</i>

23:30.120 --> 23:35.170
<i>Next episode: "A Masterful Cat 
Also Goes to Birthday Parties."</i>

23:32.680 --> 23:37.010
Can

23:32.680 --> 23:37.010
<b>A Masterful Cat Also Goes to Birthday Parties</b>

23:35.170 --> 23:36.970
<i>I am fully prepared.</i>
